# f20_std_inventory.oot — F20 HIGH product std vs ~1,030 triage
# Date: 2026-08-12
# Role: Domain Expert (inventory) — crush phalanx
# OWN: classify live `ooda/std` `.oo`. No SPRINT. No compiler. No push.

========================================================================
PLAIN ENGLISH (RULES 1.10)
========================================================================

**What is true**
Product `ooda/std` has **34** `.oo` files on disk. All 34 are git-tracked.
The ~1,030 figure is **not** a live count. It is a stale org-`std/`
triage snapshot from deleted `audit/std_triage_2026-08-11.oot`
(2026-08-11: ~646 untracked `.oo` + 223 modified + already-tracked
remainder, rounded). Do **not** invent 1,030 product files.

**Why it matters**
Comparing 31 product files to ~1,030 as if they were the same tree
is pride (SINS #3). Agents would import a library that is not there.

**What is not done**
RFC-002 args/walk still absent. Org domain trees are not the product
floor. This ledger classifies; it does not ship modules.

